  "domain": "tier0/export/processing",
  "description": "Decision 272's tie-order sweep (phase1.25_pilot-wand item 2.7: which of two equal 1/d shares leads the infinite ring's lerp chain), exploratory: 304 straight 8- and 16-texel strips (rows and columns, one quad each) whose ring texels' two diagonals tie: strips straddling the binades of the normalised and world positions along x and along z, k-ulp translations (k = 0..15) across and along at three bases, a y control, uniform and per-axis scales, and every diagonal, vertex rotation and face order; the centred mesh with its box anchors at +-320 cm, so that the normalised binades no longer sit on world binades; each copy its own 3D piece and UV island; document resolution 512. User0-User7 added as RGB32F (a record whose template capture shows one of them not 32F is void); one fill with the eight channels active, Normal at opacity 1, default projection (read back), sources the authored float32 kernel code at the document size: User0-User2 one-hot the nine classes x mod 3 + 3 (y mod 3) of the texel (column x, row y from the top), User3 the UV ramp R = (x + 0.5)/N, G = (y + 0.5)/N, B = 0.5, User4 and User5 the periodic codes d and e (k/256, one 17 x 13 texel tile each), User6 (d + e)/2 and User7 1 - d. The eight maps at OpenEXR 32f with infinite padding and with passthrough (every covered texel must equal its source bit for bit, or the probe is void), every export step done twice in the session.",
